export const PRIVACY_POLICY_MARKDOWN = {
  "en": "Effective date: 2026-10-31\n\nThis policy explains how creds (creds.id), provided by the Solid(ar)ity project (“we”), handles information when you visit, publish a page, use the creds app, or contact us. The app shows this same policy. Local-first means some work and storage happen on your device; online features also use servers.\n\n## 1. Features and versions\n\nThe information processed depends on the features you use. Viewing a page does not by itself create a name-directory entry, connect a passkey, publish a check, or enable mobile backups. Features differ by platform. The website supports public pages, creating an identity with a passkey, and passkey sign-in. The creds app, version 2.0 and later for iPhone and Android, adds the features described in sections 4 and 7 to 9. Earlier app versions, published under the Solid(ar)ity name, worked differently; this policy describes version 2.0 and later.\n\n## 2. Public pages and Nostr relays\n\nWhen you publish, the profile fields you include, such as your display name, bio, links and listed identities, become public together with public identifiers, signatures and signing times. A linked Nostr profile may also publish your creds.id name and identity binding. Checks and statements you choose to publish are public too; section 4 describes them. Do not publish information you want to keep private or information about others without authority.\n\nPublic pages are distributed through public Nostr relays. Visitors and apps request public keys and events to retrieve and check pages; relay operators can see these requests and the connecting IP address. Others may copy, index or retain public content. Updating a page, closing a QR screen, signing out or requesting deletion does not recall copies already shared.\n\n## 3. The name directory\n\nIf you claim or manage a creds.id name, the directory processes the name, public key, relay list, status, timestamps and any rename or redirect information. The public name lookup exposes the name-to-key binding and relay information. Reserved names and records of released names may be kept to prevent misuse or reassignment.\n\nDirectory operation logs record registrations, releases and recoveries, including signed requests, and have a 90-day retention period. This period applies to operation logs, not to active or retained name records, public relay copies, or hosting logs.\n\n## 4. Link checks, witnesses and passport statements\n\nWhen the app checks a link on a page, your phone fetches that public profile or website itself and looks for the page owner’s creds.id marker. The site you check sees a request from your phone, including your IP address. Nothing is published unless you choose to.\n\nIf you add a green check to your own link or tap “witness” on someone else’s page, the app publishes a signed statement to public Nostr relays. It names the link checked, the creds.id name, the page owner’s public key, your own public key and when your phone looked. Anyone can then see that you checked that page. It also carries a device proof: an attestation from Apple (App Attest) or Google (Android Key Attestation) that a genuine creds app on real hardware made it. Getting that attestation contacts Apple or Google; it shows a genuine app and device, not who you are, and it is not a count of distinct people.\n\nIf you scan a passport with the app on a phone that has NFC, the chip is read over NFC and checked on your phone; the passport’s name, number, photo and other chip data are not sent to us or published. You may then publish a passport statement, signed by your device key, that says a chip passing passive authentication was read for your public key, whether the holder was over 18, and when it was read and signed. The app re-signs it about every 30 days. Only if you opt in to being counted does it include a passport nullifier, a value derived from the chip that the issuing state or anyone holding the chip data could compute and link to your public key.\n\nPublished checks and statements are public copies like the rest of your page; replacing or withdrawing one does not recall copies others already hold. Pages viewed on the website check these statements in your browser; to check Android revocation, the website fetches Google’s public revocation list through creds.id.\n\n## 5. Hosting and request information\n\nThe website and online services use cloud hosting, including Cloudflare. creds.id also relays a few public resources for the website, such as YouTube channel feeds and thumbnails and Google’s attestation revocation list, so your browser does not contact those hosts for them. Serving requests and protecting these services can involve IP addresses, requested URLs, request times, browser or device information and operational or security logs. This information supports delivery, troubleshooting, rate limiting and abuse prevention. Local-first does not remove this network processing.\n\n## 6. Browser storage and passkeys\n\nThe current website stores page drafts, draft ownership or source information, and language and theme preferences in local storage. Drafts can remain after you leave the page and are not an encrypted backup. Older web versions may also have left passkey-protected identity data in IndexedDB; the current sign-in flow does not create that local vault. If you create an identity on the website and its upload has not finished, a passkey-sealed copy waits in local storage until it is sent. Clearing site data removes local copies, not remote records or your passkey provider’s copies.\n\nWhen you create an identity on the website with a compatible passkey, such as one from Apple or Google, the recovery phrase is generated in the browser, sealed with key material from that passkey, and uploaded to creds.id as an encrypted root-vault record. When you sign in, the browser requests that record from an address derived from the passkey credential, decrypts it locally and uses the unlocked identity in memory to sign. Passkeys of one identity are linked by an owner index that lets you list, rename and remove them; creds.id stores the encrypted records, a passkey-derived index key and the passkey names you choose. A passkey provider may sync the passkey under its own settings and policy. Support cannot replace a lost recovery phrase or promise recovery from a lost passkey.\n\n## 7. Mobile identity and the encrypted root vault\n\nIn the creds app, identity material is kept in device secure storage. Connecting a passkey uploads an encrypted vault containing the recovery phrase and, where applicable, a Nostr signing key stored separately on the device, to creds.id. The service stores ciphertext and a passkey-derived storage address; decryption is designed to happen on your device using the passkey. This encrypted identity copy enables the web sign-in described above and is separate from a backup of contacts or cards.\n\nOn iPhone, the app may also keep a recovery copy in iCloud Keychain. Device secure storage, iCloud Keychain and the creds.id root vault are distinct storage locations. Encryption reduces exposure; it is not a guarantee against every compromise or loss.\n\n## 8. Optional mobile backups and other app features\n\nCloud backup in the app is off by default. If enabled, encrypted copies of cards, contacts, attestations, profile and page data go to your own iCloud Drive or Google Drive, depending on the platform, and may support device sync. These data backups exclude identity keys and require the relevant recovery material. On iPhone, a backup may remain in app storage when iCloud Drive is unavailable. Manage cloud copies through the relevant provider.\n\nIf you use contact, card or attestation features, the app stores that information locally and processes selected information when you share or export it. Refreshing saved public pages queries relays for their public keys, and the Recent Updates list is worked out on your phone. Importing from your phone’s contacts reads them only after you grant permission. The camera reads QR codes and a passport’s machine-readable zone on the device. Device permissions and provider settings affect these optional features.\n\nPrivate card exchange (Pear) connects your phone directly to the other person’s phone over a peer-to-peer network when you start or accept an exchange. The other phone and the network’s nodes see your IP address; the card you approve is sent only to that person. You can turn private exchange off in Settings.\n\n## 9. In-app purchases\n\ncreds Pro, the app’s optional paid plan, is bought through the App Store or Google Play. The store handles payment and keeps your payment details; we do not receive them. To unlock Pro, the app sends creds.id your identity’s public identifier (did:key), your platform and the store’s purchase identifier, signed by your identity, and receives a short-lived license. creds.id checks that purchase with Apple or Google.\n\nWith Pro, you can ask the creds.id notary to witness your page. The app sends it your signed public page, its name and your license; the notary fetches your linked public profiles itself and publishes its own statement to public relays, as described in section 4.\n\n## 10. Support messages\n\nIf you email gm@solidarity.gg, we and our email provider process your email address, message, attachments and related correspondence to answer and handle your request. Send only what is needed. Never send a recovery phrase, private key or passkey secret. Correspondence is kept as needed for support, security and applicable legal obligations.\n\nWhen something fails, the app can draft an error report email to err@solidarity.gg. Nothing is sent unless you send it from your mail app. The draft contains the error message, code and technical trace, the app version, your platform and system version, and a short label for the screen; it does not include your cards, contacts or credentials. You can read and edit it before sending.\n\n## 11. Cookies, advertising and analytics\n\nThe current website does not set application cookies or include advertising, visitor analytics or tracking scripts. It uses the browser storage described above, and serves its fonts with the site. The app has no advertising or analytics either. A YouTube or Spotify item on a page loads only after you tap it; the player then comes from youtube-nocookie.com or open.spotify.com under their own policies. Hosting and security request processing still occurs. Third-party sites, relays, passkey providers and optional cloud services apply their own policies and may use their own storage or cookies.\n\n## 12. Third parties and international processing\n\nDepending on the page or feature, your device may contact public relays, name directories, DNS resolvers, Ethereum name-resolution services, Bluesky servers, the websites and profiles you check, Apple and Google for device attestation and store purchases, peers in a private exchange, or other linked services. They receive the requests needed for that function, including your IP address. Following an external link connects you to that site. These operators control their own processing.\n\nHosting, email, public relays, app stores and optional backup or passkey services may process information in other countries, whose protections can differ from those where you live. Public content may be distributed worldwide. We may disclose information under our control when required by applicable law or as necessary to address abuse or protect legal rights.\n\n## 13. Your choices, rights and deletion limits\n\nYou can choose what to publish, edit information where supported, clear browser storage, and manage device permissions and provider backups. We retain service records as needed to operate and secure the relevant feature or meet applicable legal obligations; the directory-log period is specified above. Uninstalling an app or clearing a browser does not erase every copy, and some app resets preserve identity keys.\n\nDepending on applicable law, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or receive a copy of information, restrict or object to processing, withdraw consent where processing relies on it, or complain to the relevant data-protection authority. Contact gm@solidarity.gg with your request. We may need proportionate verification of your authority. We handle requests in accordance with applicable legal requirements.\n\nYou can remove a passkey and its encrypted vault record in passkey management on the website or in the app, and delete your whole account as described in section 14. Contact us about other records under our control; this contact route does not itself delete them. Published checks, witnesses and passport statements are public relay copies. We cannot guarantee removal from independent relays, recipients, caches or other copies outside our control. Cloud backups and passkey-provider copies must also be managed with those providers.\n\n## 14. Deleting your account\n\nIn the creds app (version 2.0 and later), go to Settings, then Delete account. After you confirm with Face ID or your device passcode, the app uses keys that exist only on your phone to: publish empty replacements and Nostr deletion requests for the page, checks and witness statements the app published under your key, and remove the creds.id name and identity binding the app added to your Nostr profile (other fields you set elsewhere are left as they are); unlink every creds.id name your key held and delete its directory operation logs; delete every encrypted root-vault record in your owner index, including passkeys added on the website; delete the link between your creds Pro purchase and your identity; delete any messages still held for you by the retired Shoutouts inbox; and finally erase identity keys, cards, contacts, credentials and settings on the phone. If any online step fails, the app says which one, keeps your keys on the phone and lets you retry; it never reports the account as deleted until every step has succeeded.\n\nWithout the app, see creds.id/delete-account, or email gm@solidarity.gg from the address you want us to reply to, with your creds.id name and the public key (npub) of the account. Because our records are tied to keys rather than to accounts with passwords, we may ask you to prove control of that key, for example by publishing a short statement we specify; we act within 30 days. Without the keys we can unlink a name and remove a page from our own services, but we cannot sign Nostr deletion requests on your behalf.\n\nWhat stays, and why: a deleted name remains reserved permanently as a record linked to no key, so nobody else can register it and impersonate your old page. It cannot be reclaimed afterwards, not even with your old key. Public relays are operated by others; most honour deletion requests, but we cannot guarantee it, and copies already fetched by visitors, apps, caches or the people you shared cards or statements with cannot be recalled. Hosting and security logs follow their own short retention. Backups in your iCloud Drive, Google Drive or iCloud Keychain, a recovery phrase you exported, and passkeys held by your passkey provider are under your control; remove them there.\n\nDeleting your account does not cancel a creds Pro subscription. Cancel it in the App Store or Google Play subscription settings; otherwise the store keeps billing you. Apple and Google keep their own purchase records under their policies.\n\n## 15. Minors\n\ncreds is not directed at children. If you are below the age at which you can independently agree to use the service where you live, involve a parent or guardian as required by law. Avoid publishing a minor’s personal information. Contact us if you believe information about a child has been shared improperly so we can assess steps within our control.\n\n## 16. Changes and contact\n\nWe may update this policy as the service changes. The effective date identifies this version. We will publish updates here and provide additional notice or obtain consent when applicable law requires it. Questions and privacy requests can be sent to gm@solidarity.gg.\n\ngm@solidarity.gg · https://creds.id/privacy\n",
  "zh-Hant": "生效日： 2026-10-31\n\n本政策說明由 Solid(ar)ity project（以下稱「我們」）提供的 creds（creds.id），如何在你瀏覽、發布頁面、使用 creds App 或聯絡我們時處理資訊。App 內顯示的也是這份政策。Local-first 表示部分運算與儲存在你的裝置上進行；線上功能仍會使用伺服器。\n\n## 1. 功能與版本\n\n處理哪些資訊取決於你使用的功能。單純瀏覽頁面不會自動建立名稱目錄紀錄、連接 passkey、發布查驗或啟用手機備份。功能依平台而異。網站支援公開頁面、以 passkey 建立身分及 passkey 登入。creds App 2.0 以上版本（iPhone 與 Android）另提供第 4 節及第 7 至 9 節所述的功能。較早以 Solid(ar)ity 名稱發布的 App 版本運作方式不同；本政策描述的是 2.0 以上版本。\n\n## 2. 公開頁面與 Nostr relays\n\n發布時，你加入的個人資料欄位，例如顯示名稱、簡介、連結與列出的身分，會與公開識別碼、簽章及簽署時間一併公開。連接的 Nostr 個人資料也可能公布你的 creds.id 名稱與身分綁定。你選擇發布的查驗與聲明同樣公開，詳見第 4 節。請勿發布你想保密的資訊，或未經授權發布他人的資訊。\n\n公開頁面透過 Nostr 公共 relays 傳遞。訪客與 App 會查詢公開金鑰和事件，以取得及查驗頁面；relay 營運者可看到這些查詢與連線 IP 位址。他人可能複製、建立索引或保留公開內容。更新頁面、關閉 QR 畫面、登出或提出刪除請求，都不會收回已分享的副本。\n\n## 3. 名稱目錄\n\n如果你申請或管理 creds.id 名稱，目錄會處理名稱、公開金鑰、relay 清單、狀態、時間戳記及改名或重新導向資訊。公開名稱查詢會提供名稱與金鑰的綁定及 relay 資訊。為防止濫用或重新分配，保留名稱與已釋放名稱的紀錄可能持續保留。\n\n目錄操作記錄包含註冊、釋放及恢復操作與簽署請求，保存期間為 90 天。這個期間適用於操作記錄，不適用於有效或保留的名稱紀錄、公共 relay 副本或主機服務記錄。\n\n## 4. 連結查驗、見證與護照聲明\n\nApp 查驗頁面上的連結時，由你的手機自己抓取該公開個人資料或網站，尋找頁面擁有者的 creds.id 標記。被查驗的網站會看到來自你手機的請求，包括你的 IP 位址。除非你選擇發布，不會公開任何內容。\n\n當你替自己的連結加上綠勾，或在別人的頁面按「見證」，App 會將一則簽署聲明發布到 Nostr 公共 relays。聲明包含被查驗的連結、creds.id 名稱、頁面擁有者的公開金鑰、你自己的公開金鑰，以及你的手機查看的時間；任何人都能看到你查驗過那個頁面。聲明也附帶裝置證明：Apple（App Attest）或 Google（Android Key Attestation）出具的、證明它由真機上未經修改的 creds App 產生的 attestation。取得 attestation 時會連線 Apple 或 Google；它證明的是正版 App 與真實裝置，不是你是誰，也不能用來計算不同的人數。\n\n用 App 在有 NFC 的手機上掃描護照時，晶片透過 NFC 讀取並在你的手機上查驗；護照上的姓名、號碼、照片及其他晶片資料不會傳給我們，也不會公開。之後你可以發布一則由裝置金鑰簽署的護照聲明，內容是：一個通過 passive authentication 的晶片已針對你的公開金鑰讀取、持有人是否年滿 18 歲，以及讀取與簽署時間。App 約每 30 天重新簽署一次。只有在你選擇被計入時，聲明才會包含護照 nullifier；這是由晶片資料衍生的值，發照國或任何持有晶片資料的人都能算出並連結到你的公開金鑰。\n\n已發布的查驗與聲明，和你頁面的其他內容一樣是公開副本；替換或撤回不會收回他人已持有的副本。在網站上瀏覽頁面時，這些聲明由你的瀏覽器查驗；為了檢查 Android 金鑰是否被撤銷，網站會透過 creds.id 取得 Google 的公開撤銷清單。\n\n## 5. 主機服務與請求資訊\n\n網站與線上服務使用包括 Cloudflare 在內的雲端主機。creds.id 也替網站轉送少數公開資源，例如 YouTube 頻道列表與縮圖，以及 Google 的 attestation 撤銷清單，所以你的瀏覽器不必為此連線這些主機。傳送請求及保護服務的過程可能涉及 IP 位址、請求網址、請求時間、瀏覽器或裝置資訊，以及運作或安全記錄。這些資訊用於提供服務、排查問題、限制請求頻率及防止濫用。Local-first 不代表沒有這些網路處理。\n\n## 6. 瀏覽器儲存與 passkey\n\n目前網站使用 local storage 儲存頁面草稿、草稿擁有者或來源資訊，以及語言與主題偏好。草稿可能在離開頁面後繼續保留，且不是加密備份。舊版網站也可能在 IndexedDB 留下受 passkey 保護的身分資料；目前登入流程不會建立該本機 vault。如果你在網站上建立身分而上傳尚未完成，一份以 passkey 封存的副本會留在 local storage，直到送出。清除網站資料會移除本機副本，不會刪除遠端紀錄或 passkey 供應商的副本。\n\n在網站上以相容的 passkey（例如 Apple 或 Google 的 passkey）建立身分時，恢復詞在瀏覽器中產生，以該 passkey 衍生的金鑰資料封存後，作為加密 root vault 紀錄上傳至 creds.id。登入時，瀏覽器依 passkey 憑證衍生的位址請求該紀錄，在本機解密，並在記憶體中使用已解鎖的身分簽署。同一身分的多把 passkey 以擁有者索引相連，讓你列出、重新命名及移除；creds.id 儲存加密紀錄、由 passkey 衍生的索引金鑰，以及你取的 passkey 名稱。Passkey 供應商可能依其設定與政策同步 passkey。客服無法替換遺失的恢復詞，也不能保證在 passkey 遺失後恢復存取。\n\n## 7. 手機身分與加密 root vault\n\ncreds App 會將身分金鑰資料保存在裝置的安全儲存空間。連接 passkey 時，會將包含恢復詞，以及適用時在裝置上另外儲存的 Nostr 簽署金鑰的完整加密 vault，上傳至 creds.id。服務儲存密文與依 passkey 衍生的儲存位址；設計上由你的裝置使用 passkey 解密。這份加密身分副本用於前述網站登入，與聯絡人或名片的資料備份不同。\n\n在 iPhone 上，App 也可能在 iCloud Keychain 保留恢復副本。裝置安全儲存空間、iCloud Keychain 與 creds.id root vault 是不同的儲存位置。加密可降低資料暴露的風險，但不保證防止所有入侵或遺失情況。\n\n## 8. 選用的手機備份與其他 App 功能\n\nApp 的雲端備份預設不啟用。啟用後，名片、聯絡人、證明、個人資料及頁面的加密副本，會依平台存入你自己的 iCloud Drive 或 Google Drive，也可能用於裝置間同步。這些資料備份不含身分金鑰，且需要相應的恢復資料。iPhone 無法使用 iCloud Drive 時，備份可能留在 App 儲存空間。請透過相應的供應商管理雲端副本。\n\n如果使用聯絡人、名片或證明功能，App 會在本機儲存相關資訊，並在你分享或匯出時處理所選資訊。更新已儲存的公開頁面時，會向 relays 查詢其公開金鑰；「最近更新」清單在你的手機上計算。從手機通訊錄匯入時，只有在你授權後才會讀取。相機在裝置上讀取 QR code 與護照的機讀區。裝置權限及供應商設定會影響這些選用功能。\n\n私密名片交換（Pear）會在你發起或接受交換時，透過點對點網路讓你的手機直接連到對方手機。對方手機與該網路的節點會看到你的 IP 位址；你核准的名片只傳給那個人。你可以在設定中關閉私密交換。\n\n## 9. App 內購買\n\ncreds Pro 是 App 的選用付費方案，透過 App Store 或 Google Play 購買。付款由商店處理並保存你的付款資料，我們不會收到。為了開通 Pro，App 會把你身分的公開識別碼（did:key）、平台與商店的購買識別碼，以你的身分簽署後送到 creds.id，換取一張短期授權；creds.id 會向 Apple 或 Google 確認該筆購買。\n\n有 Pro 時，你可以請 creds.id notary 見證你的頁面。App 會送出你已簽署的公開頁面、名稱與授權；notary 自己抓取你連結的公開個人資料，並將它自己的聲明發布到公共 relays，如第 4 節所述。\n\n## 10. 客服訊息\n\n當你寄信至 gm@solidarity.gg，我們與電子郵件供應商會處理你的電子郵件地址、訊息、附件及相關往來，以回覆及處理請求。請僅提供必要資訊，切勿寄送恢復詞、私鑰或 passkey 機密資料。我們會依客服、安全及適用法律義務所需保留往來紀錄。\n\n發生錯誤時，App 可以草擬一封寄到 err@solidarity.gg 的錯誤回報信。除非你從郵件 App 寄出，否則不會傳送。草稿包含錯誤訊息、代碼與技術追蹤、App 版本、你的平台與系統版本，以及畫面的簡短標籤；不包含你的名片、聯絡人或憑證。寄出前你可以閱讀與修改。\n\n## 11. Cookies、廣告與分析\n\n目前網站不設定應用程式 cookies，也不加入廣告、訪客分析或追蹤腳本。網站使用前述瀏覽器儲存空間，並隨網站提供字型。App 也沒有廣告或分析。頁面上的 YouTube 或 Spotify 項目在你點按後才載入，播放器之後由 youtube-nocookie.com 或 open.spotify.com 提供，適用其自身政策。主機服務及安全所需的請求處理仍會發生。第三方網站、relays、passkey 供應商及選用雲端服務適用各自的政策，也可能使用自己的儲存空間或 cookies。\n\n## 12. 第三方與跨境處理\n\n依頁面或功能不同，你的裝置可能連接公共 relays、名稱目錄、DNS 解析服務、Ethereum 名稱解析服務、Bluesky 伺服器、你查驗的網站與個人資料、提供裝置 attestation 與商店購買的 Apple 和 Google、私密交換中的對方，或其他連結服務。這些服務會收到該功能所需的請求，包括你的 IP 位址。開啟外部連結會連接至該網站。這些營運者自行管理其資料處理。\n\n主機服務、電子郵件、公共 relays、App 商店，以及選用的備份或 passkey 服務，可能在其他國家處理資訊，其保護程度可能與你所在地不同。公開內容可能傳送至全球各地。我們可能依適用法律要求，或在處理濫用及保護合法權利所必要的範圍內，揭露我們控制的資訊。\n\n## 13. 你的選擇、權利與刪除限制\n\n你可以選擇發布內容、在支援的功能中修改資訊、清除瀏覽器儲存空間，以及管理裝置權限與供應商備份。我們依營運及保護相關功能或履行適用法律義務所需保留服務紀錄；目錄操作記錄的期間已於前文說明。移除 App 或清除瀏覽器不會刪除所有副本，部分 App 重設操作也會保留身分金鑰。\n\n依適用法律，你可能享有查閱、更正、刪除、取得資訊副本、限制或反對處理、在以同意為依據時撤回同意，或向相關資料保護主管機關申訴的權利。請寄信至 gm@solidarity.gg 提出請求。我們可能需要以適當方式核實你的權限，並依適用法律要求處理。\n\n你可以在網站或 App 的 passkey 管理中，移除一把 passkey 及其加密 vault 紀錄，也可以依第 14 節刪除整個帳號。關於我們控制的其他紀錄，請聯絡我們；聯絡本身不會直接刪除紀錄。已發布的查驗、見證與護照聲明屬於公共 relay 副本。我們無法保證從獨立 relays、收件人、快取或其他不受我們控制的副本移除資訊。雲端備份與 passkey 供應商副本，也必須透過該供應商管理。\n\n## 14. 刪除你的帳號\n\n在 creds App（2.0 以上版本）中，前往「設定」→「刪除帳號」。以 Face ID 或裝置密碼確認後，App 會用只存在你手機上的金鑰：為 App 以你的金鑰發布的頁面、查驗與見證聲明發布空白取代版本與 Nostr 刪除請求，並從你的 Nostr 個人檔案移除 App 加入的 creds.id 名稱與身分綁定（你在其他地方設定的欄位不會變動）；解除你的金鑰持有過的所有 creds.id 名稱連結，並刪除其目錄操作記錄；刪除 owner index 中所有加密 root vault 紀錄，包括在網站上新增的 passkey；刪除 creds Pro 購買與你身分之間的連結；刪除已停用的 Shoutouts 收件匣中仍為你保留的訊息；最後清除手機上的身分金鑰、名片、聯絡人、憑證與設定。任何線上步驟失敗時，App 會指出是哪一步、把金鑰留在手機上並讓你重試；在所有步驟成功之前，絕不會顯示帳號已刪除。\n\n沒有 App 時，請參閱 creds.id/delete-account，或從你希望我們回覆的信箱寄信至 gm@solidarity.gg，附上你的 creds.id 名稱與帳號公鑰（npub）。因為我們的紀錄綁定的是金鑰而非有密碼的帳號，我們可能請你證明你控制該金鑰，例如發布一段我們指定的簡短聲明；我們會在 30 天內處理。沒有金鑰時，我們可以解除名稱連結並從我們自己的服務移除頁面，但無法代你簽署 Nostr 刪除請求。\n\n會保留的內容與原因：已刪除的名稱會以不連結任何金鑰的紀錄永久保留，避免他人註冊後冒充你過去的頁面；之後無法取回，即使使用舊金鑰也不行。公共 relays 由他人營運，多數會遵守刪除請求，但我們無法保證；訪客、應用程式、快取，或你分享過名片與聲明的對象已取得的副本無法收回。主機與安全記錄依其各自的短期保存期間處理。你的 iCloud Drive、Google 雲端硬碟或 iCloud 鑰匙圈備份、你匯出的復原詞，以及 passkey 供應商保存的 passkey 由你控制，請在該處移除。\n\n刪除帳號不會取消 creds Pro 訂閱。請在 App Store 或 Google Play 的訂閱設定中取消，否則商店會繼續收費。Apple 與 Google 會依其政策保留自己的購買紀錄。\n\n## 15. 未成年人\n\ncreds 並非以兒童為服務對象。如果你未達所在地可自行同意使用服務的年齡，請依法律要求由家長或監護人參與。請避免發布未成年人的個人資訊。如果你認為兒童資訊遭到不當分享，請聯絡我們，以便評估我們控制範圍內可採取的措施。\n\n## 16. 政策變更與聯絡\n\n我們可能隨服務變更更新本政策，生效日用於識別此版本。我們會在此發布更新，並在適用法律要求時另行通知或取得同意。政策問題與隱私請求請寄至 gm@solidarity.gg。\n\ngm@solidarity.gg · https://creds.id/privacy\n",
} as const;
